## Maintenance
On any screen-pattern change: update `skills/screens.md`, then commit + push. On a {{SYSTEM_NAME}}
republish: refresh the 3 read-only skill mirrors (`cp ../{{DS_REPO}}/skills/<f> skills/<f>`,
re-add the header), bump the consumed-version line in `CONTEXT.md`, **then run `consumer-migrator`
(`/rebind`) to propagate the change across the consumer file + verify it's actually consumed**, commit + push.

## Agent orchestration ({{SYSTEM_NAME}} screen-creation agents)

This context is **screen + prototype only** — two core role-based subagents (`product-designer`,
`ui-designer`) + supporting (`art-director` = creative direction, `flow-reviewer` = independent
usability review, `behavioral-scientist` = independent evidence + ethics review, `consumer-migrator` =
migration), plus `data-analyst` for the empirical loop. On any task, decide the moment in the pipeline
first, then delegate. Full map, pipeline, and operating rules: see `AGENTS-HANDOFF.md`.

| Route to | When | Write surface |
|---|---|---|
| `product-designer` | deconstruct the ask (business goal · metric · segment · JTBD · constraints · scope · CX criteria), then flows, IA, state matrices, interaction/a11y specs, research synthesis, acceptance criteria, functional microcopy — the brief, BEFORE pixels; runs the usability-validation gate | specs only (no pixels) |
| `art-director` *(optional)* | creative direction from a reference/trend (the `visual-craft` canon) — deconstruct → filter through the token/brand fence → adapt-not-copy → 2–3 named directions → low-fi `Explorations` frames; hands a build spec to `ui-designer` | consumer file `Explorations / <flow>` (low-fi only) |
| `ui-designer` | compose {{SYSTEM_NAME}} into pixel-perfect consumer screens, build-time design-review self-check, consumer drift sweep | consumer file `{{CONSUMER_FIGMA_KEY}}` |
| `flow-reviewer` | INDEPENDENT heuristic evaluation of screens + flows (the `ux-flow-review` canon) — the usability gate | read-only review |
| `behavioral-scientist` | INDEPENDENT mechanism + anti-manipulation gate (the `behavioral-science-principles.md` evidence base) — feeds `product-designer` | read-only review; owns the principles doc |
| `consumer-migrator` | propagate a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish across consumer files (the `rebind` procedure) — confirm changes are consumed | consumer file(s) |
| `data-analyst` | turn prototype analytics into screen-validation evidence (the `usability-analytics` canon) — feeds `product-designer` | read-only analysis |
| _separate context_ | author tokens/components/variants, publish {{SYSTEM_NAME}}, drift, manifest, spiels | NOT handled here — `{{DS_REPO}}` (`ds-steward` / `component-designer` / `brand-designer`) |
| `usability-prototype` skill | build/instrument the coded prototype + run the **required usability gate** before handoff | `prototypes/` (React/Vite) |

**The intake→define→(direct)→build→validate→handoff pipeline:** `product-designer` deconstructs the ask
(business goal · metric · segment · JTBD · constraints · scope · CX criteria) and defines the brief
(flows + state matrix + acceptance criteria + functional copy) → *optionally* `art-director` sets an
on-brand visual direction from a reference/trend (the `visual-craft` canon) → `ui-designer` composes
{{SYSTEM_NAME}} into the screen and clears the two Figma gates → `flow-reviewer` runs the independent heuristic
evaluation → the flow is **usability-tested as a coded prototype** → `data-analyst` benchmarks the
behavior (the `usability-analytics` canon) → `product-designer` **validates** the screens against that
evidence, against the business goal AND CX → the **validated** screens hand off to product + engineering /
go live. A {{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap → request to the DS context, never a hand-built equivalent.

**Shared building blocks** keep the system honest:
- **`ux-flow-review` skill** — the single heuristic-evaluation canon (5 frameworks + {{DOMAIN}} + WCAG
  2.2 AA). `ui-designer` (self-check), `flow-reviewer` (gate), and `/design-review` all load it — no
  restating the frameworks anywhere, or they drift.
- **`behavioral-science-principles.md` + `behavioral-scientist` agent** — the evidence + ethics gate.
  This project's behavioral mechanisms → screen patterns, their strong-vs-suggestive calibration, and
  the anti-pattern (dark-pattern) refusal list. The doc is single-sourced by the agent; the
  `ux-flow-review` {{DOMAIN}} overlay and `/behavioral-review` cite it — evidence changes there, never
  restated. Complementary to the usability gate: it asks *why does this work and is it honest*,
  `flow-reviewer` asks *can they use it*.
- **`visual-craft` skill + `art-director` agent** — the creative-direction canon (deconstruct →
  filter through the token/brand fence → adapt-not-copy → 2–3 named directions → low-fi Explorations).
  The optional stage between `product-designer` and `ui-designer`; run via `/art-direction`. Aesthetics
  never overrides usability/a11y, and a new-component need is a DS gap, never a hand-build.
- **`usability-analytics` skill + `data-analyst` agent** — the empirical validation loop. Turns the
  prototype's PostHog/Clarity/SEQ instrumentation into benchmarked evidence (task success / time /
  SEQ / drop-off vs UX norms, quant triangulated with Clarity replays) so the `product-designer`
  validates screens with DATA, not opinion. Expert review (`ux-flow-review`) + empirical data are complementary.
- **`rebind` skill + `consumer-migrator` agent** — the consume-verification loop. After a DS
  publish, swap stale consumer instances onto the fresh main (Gotcha #20), rebind overrides
  (#21/#28), re-audit (#27/#28), verify. This is how we KNOW a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} change is actually being used.
- **`flow-layout` skill** — section/frame auto-layout by flow name; `ui-designer` runs it via `/relayout`.
- **`figma-versioning` skill** (★ cross-cutting, **no agent of its own**) — named version-history
  checkpoints on the consumer file, folded into `ui-designer` (`pre-build:` / `gate-pass:`),
  `consumer-migrator` (`pre-rebind:` — the load-bearing one, before the instance swap), and
  `art-director` (before writing Explorations); invoked directly via `/checkpoint` + `/changelog`.

Operating rules (full detail in AGENTS-HANDOFF.md):
- Plan Mode is the gate before any consumer-file write — plan in `yaml` (instances + keys + bindings
  + honest gaps), approve, then build incrementally with render-verification.
- Load `skills/*.md` + `DESIGN.md` fresh, never from memory. Refresh the read-only DS mirrors after a
  {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish.
- Apply the `DESIGN.md` §6 heuristic canon at the **screen + flow layer** (mapping in
  `AGENTS-HANDOFF.md`) — the system/component slices belong to the DS context.

Slash commands (thin wrappers that delegate to the agents — never duplicate the workflow, or it drifts):
`/design-review` (→ flow-reviewer) · `/behavioral-review` (→ behavioral-scientist) · `/consumer-audit` (→ ui-designer) · `/art-direction` (→ art-director) · `/rebind` (→ consumer-migrator) · `/usability-report` (→ data-analyst) · `/relayout` (→ ui-designer, runs flow-layout) · `/checkpoint` + `/changelog` (→ figma-versioning)
